Shanling Q2 tools
=================

The Q2 runs Linux 5.10 on an Ingenic X2000 (MIPS32r2, nan2008) with glibc 2.28 and no IPv6.
q2-soulseek runs from the card's .soulseek folder as a Q2 Pod card app (q2-pod's patch/addon.c):
Q2 Pod lists it in Streaming, starts it from that row, draws its page and keeps the Q2 awake while
files move. Nothing is flashed for it.

  build.sh     static Go for the Q2 and the card files, in target/shanlingq2/.soulseek, zipped as
               target/shanlingq2/q2-soulseek-vX.Y-SHA.zip (unzip that at the card's root)
  package.py   checks the binary (static, MIPS32 little-endian, soft-float ABI), sets the nan2008
               ELF flag the Q2's kernel requires and Go doesn't, and writes the ZIP
  launcher.sh  installed as .soulseek/run: q2-soulseek copied to /tmp and run there in a restart loop
  q2app        installed as .soulseek/q2app: the card app manifest (name=Soulseek)
  test_launcher.py
               runs launcher.sh on the host with a fake app

Install
-------

Q2 Pod's System settings -> Apps installs the latest release over Wi-Fi. By hand, unzip
q2-soulseek-*.zip from https://github.com/group-a-study/q2-soulseek/releases/latest to the card's
root with the Q2 powered off. See the top-level README.md.

Build
-----

  contrib/shanlingq2/build.sh [OUT]

Go 1.22 or later and python3; nothing outside Go's standard library. The binary is CGO_ENABLED=0
GOOS=linux GOARCH=mipsle GOMIPS=softfloat, static, so it needs none of the Q2's libraries. Tests:
go test ./... runs two clients against a fake Soulseek server (search, attributes, a resumed
download, sharing paused on battery and resumed on the cable, refusals, a firewalled connection the
other way round) and the whole app through its web API, Q2SPOT/1 page and status file; the same
tests run as MIPS code under qemu-mipsel (go test -exec qemu-mipsel). python3
contrib/shanlingq2/test_launcher.py tests the launcher. A tag q2-vX.Y matching
cmd/q2-soulseek/main.go's version publishes the release (.github/workflows/release.yml).

Device
------

Q2 Pod runs /bin/sh /mnt/mmc/.soulseek/run when Streaming's Soulseek row is pressed and it isn't
running. The launcher copies q2-soulseek and itself to /tmp and leaves the card at once; the loop
restarts it after a crash, waiting 5 s and doubling to a minute, and leaves its pid in
/tmp/q2-soulseek. An exit of 0 (stopped from the Q2 or the phone, or idle) ends the loop. A TERM to
it stops q2-soulseek cleanly, its downloads saved: Q2 Pod sends it for Stop Streaming Services,
Home's Rockbox row, an Apps update or remove, and USB storage (after which it starts it again).
Downloads are written to the card in 512 KB chunks, each file opened and closed around its write,
and shared files are read the same way, so the card is almost never busy. Its log is
/tmp/q2-soulseek.log.

  /tmp/q2-soulseek.state
      rewritten whole when it changes: state (setup, connecting, online, offline, refused,
      elsewhere), note (the line under the QR code), addr (ip:port of the phone page), pin, qr and
      qrsize (the code's rows as hex, the leftmost module the high bit of a row's first digit),
      hold (1: keep the Q2 awake), sharing (Off, On, Paused), dl, queued, done, up, version
  /tmp/q2-soulseek.sock
      the datagram q stops it
  /tmp/q2-soulseek.browse.sock
      Q2SPOT/1 (q2-pod's docs/librespot.md) for the Q2's page, below
  port 8080 (the next free one if taken)
      the phone page. The QR code carries a key that signs the browser in; typed by hand, the page
      asks for the PIN on the Q2's screen. Ten wrong PINs lock it for a minute. Settings -> On the
      Q2 -> Sign out all phones makes a new key and PIN
  .soulseek/config.json, .soulseek/downloads.json, .soulseek/shares.cache
      settings (the password as typed), the transfers and the share index; updates keep them

Network: the Soulseek server is server.slsknet.org:2242; the app logs in as an experimental client
(major version 177, as SLSKPROTOCOL.md asks of new clients). It listens on port 2234 for other users
(the next free one if taken). Behind a router without that port forwarded, other users still reach
you indirectly through the server as long as their own port is open; forwarding it brings more
results and faster connections. While sharing is on, the Q2 answers other users' searches, joins
the distributed search network as a leaf (it takes no children), and sends files from the shared
folders, upload_slots (2) at a time.

The page
--------

Each row's kind says what a press does (q2-pod's patch/addon.c): list opens the level uri (its
argument the row's context), action sends uri with the context and toasts the reply's message,
search opens the Q2's keyboard (OK asks for search <text>), remote opens the QR code, info does
nothing. A row's position, when set, is the op a held Play/Pause sends. An ok reply whose message
is refresh is asked again every 2 s while it is on top.

  menu
      Phone Remote, Search, Downloads, Uploads, Sharing, Account, Stop Soulseek; before setup,
      Set up on your phone and Stop Soulseek
  search <term> [cursor]
      the term's audio results, 50 a page; action download <search.n>, held downloadfolder
  downloads, uploads [cursor]
      a list transfer <id> row each
  transfer <id>
      its state, and Pause, Resume, Try Again, Remove
  account
      the name, status, shares and port
  set sharing
      the next sharing mode, saved
  download, downloadfolder <search.n>
      that result's file, or its folder
  pause, resume, retry, remove <id>, stop
      the transfer; the app ends
